 "end_condition_justification": "The archived 3,405-state mission (rod_steps.npz) was solved using the parallel rod model (backbone_20261108/backbone.py) with EI_rod = EI_body (44,118) + EI_backbone (20,612) = 64,730 N mm^2. Because the PA12 body and central NiTi backbone are bonded to the same rigid end disks (D0/D1) in parallel and are NOT coupled at the intermediate hub rings (8.40 mm bore vs 1.80 mm rod = 3.30 mm radial gap), both share the exact same end rotation omega_rod. Prescribing omega_rod (kinematic) on D1 of the (body + backbone) assembly is therefore directly consistent with the rod model: the backbone carries ~32-34% of the total end moment while the PA12 body carries ~66-68%, and the body's hub strain does NOT drop by 44/65 (since omega_rod already reflects the backbone's stiffening in the rod simulation). Load-controlled application of M_rod = K_rod @ omega_rod to (body + backbone) is likewise consistent and yields slightly higher strain (~6-8%) only because the solid-ring PA12 lattice is slightly more compliant than the 44,118 N mm^2 database value.",
